--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
static assertion failed
is unknown$
dropped the body
--
N5008 [temp.inst]/3, [temp.mem]: a member class template of a class template
specialization is instantiated in the context of that specialization, with
the enclosing class's template parameters bound to its arguments.  The
front end reads those bindings from the enclosing instance's class symbol,
but recorded them there only AFTER the instance's body had been converted;
a static data member's in-class initializer that instantiates the member
template (`offsetof(first_padding_byte<>, byte)') therefore found no
binding for `T', the member instance's body failed silently and stayed an
empty struct: offsetof gave 0 and, with libc++, every std::string copy
(`__constexpr_memmove', sized by `__libcpp_datasizeof<char>::value') was
one byte short -- the KNOWNBUG libcxx_string_move_ctor_lambda's second
half.  Fixed in round 163b.
